{"author":{"id":"89da5fec8eff6d69dbcdd68f81be7e9163b16f34b17e978ecf3554487379f453"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1772908084,"nonce":"B44W7Bbr0513C7PjInPCOfna168=","title":"UI remains interactive during auth-merge execution window, allowing race-condition double-approvals","message":"When auth-merge is executing (status: approved → executing → build → restart), the Mandible UI is still fully interactive. The user can approve a second auth request during this window. Since auth-merge runs in the daemon process, a second approval while the daemon is mid-restart or mid-build causes the second request to get stuck in \"approved\" with no output and no exit code.\n\nThe rebuilding splash only appears after the daemon restarts and the browser polls /api/health — too late to prevent the race.\n\nExpected behavior: as soon as any auth request transitions to \"approved/executing\", the UI should become non-interactive (or at minimum the auth queue should be locked) until the operation completes or fails. The YubiKey touch/PIN interaction must remain possible.\n\nObserved: user approved feature/issue-fetch-and-backfill-fix (which triggered a Mandible self-merge + rebuild), then immediately approved feature/attempt-tracking-policy before the splash appeared. Second request stuck at status=approved indefinitely.\n\nWorkaround: PUT /api/auth/request/\u003cid\u003e with status=pending to reset.","files":null}]}